            "The **you (pl)** form (־תֶּם) shifts the stress and shortens the first vowel: כְּתַבְתֶּם, not כָּתַבְתֶּם. In everyday speech many Israelis ignore the shift and say כָּתַבְתֶּם — and nobody minds."
